The train arrived at the station.
I quickly got into the train.
I got a window seat.
I sat in that seat.
After a while, a family came and sat opposite me.
It was a father, a mother, and a small boy.
That boy had a big bag in his hand.
The bag was very heavy.
His mother tried to help him.
She tried to take his bag.
But he did not give that bag to her.
"This is my own bag," he said.
He carried his own bag alone.
He put it on the seat with great difficulty.
His mother smiled seeing that.
I also looked at that boy and smiled.
After a little while, the train moved forward.
